Q: Which conventions are best for GET mapping (REST)?

REST GET URLs should be clean, consistent, resource-oriented.
HTTP method already means “read” — URL names the **resource**, not the action.

────────────────────────────────────────
1) Nouns use karein, verbs nahi

❌ /getAllUsers  /fetchUser
✅ /users

Reason: GET already = fetch.

2) Plural resource names

✅ /users
✅ /users/10

3) Hierarchy for relationships (nested resources)

✅ /users/10/orders
✅ /users/10/orders/5

Don’t over-nest (usually 2 levels is enough).

4) Filters / search → query params

✅ /users?role=admin
✅ /products?category=mobile&sort=price&page=0&size=20

Path = identity; query = filter/sort/page.

5) Hyphen preferred over underscore

✅ /user-profiles
❌ /user_profiles

6) Lowercase

✅ /user-profiles
❌ /UserProfiles

────────────────────────────────────────
Spring examples

@GetMapping("/users")
public List<User> getAllUsers() { ... }

@GetMapping("/users/{id}")
public User getUserById(@PathVariable Long id) { ... }

@GetMapping("/users/{id}/orders")
public List<Order> getUserOrders(@PathVariable Long id) { ... }

@GetMapping("/users")
public Page<User> search(
    @RequestParam(required = false) String role,
    Pageable pageable) { ... }

────────────────────────────────────────
Extra interview tips

| Do                              | Don’t                         |
| ------------------------------- | ----------------------------- |
| /api/v1/users (versioning)      | verbs in path                 |
| 200 + body for found            | send body on GET (avoid)      |
| 404 when resource missing       | encode actions like /doDelete |
| consistent plural nouns         | mix /user and /users          |

One-liner:
“GET URLs name resources in plural nouns, use path for IDs, query params for filters, and keep paths lowercase with hyphens — no verbs.”
